    "paragraph": "An analysis of 342 Chinese cities used spatial error modeling and geographical convergent cross mapping to examine how infrastructure supply intensity and spatial inequality associate with economic development. Another study utilized GDELT event data and spatial econometric models to map the spatiotemporal patterns and drivers of conflict risk in Pakistan from 2015 to 2024 at both national and provincial scales. Finally, researchers investigated the Finnish concept of \"talkoot\" through archival and case-based research in Helsinki to identify five place- and situation-specific characteristics of urban commoning.",
